==Battleground==
*1 [[Baa Baa]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~36.67 seconds<sup>800f~1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 10~23.33 seconds<sup>300f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Dagshund]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Malevolent Jamiera Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**2 [[Dolphina]]s spawn, delay 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
**4 [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Using a surge unit has a very possible chance of allowing Malevolent Jamiera's surge retaliation to perform his deadly savage blow on your entire stack of attackers and debuffers, which can lead to you losing the stage, however this can be circumvented by building your lineup around surge immune units.

Use the Dagshund at the beginning of the stage to stall for money, and build up a decently good stack of [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]]. If you don't feel like taking 20 minutes on the stage, bring a shield piercer like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] to reduce Malevolent Jamiera's effective 4 million HP. [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] is also extremely helpful here, as it can help keep Dolphina off your cyberstack.

You can also try to kill the two Dolphinas, as then stalling Malevolent Jameira would get easier with Maize + Rock and research combo.

=== Recommended Units ===
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: An extremely effective crowd controller able to keep Malevolent Jamiera in place when stacked.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: works extremely well with Cyberpunk, as it covers cyberpunk's blindspot with knockback and slow.
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cactus Cat]]: Helpful meatshield here, with its strong vs aku ability. Furthermore, he is surge immune, allowing for synergy with Uril.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]]: Basically a better version of Cactus, at level 50 Maize can survive multiple hits from Malevolent Jamiera provided it doesn't perform its savage blow. However, Maize drops from a pretty difficult brutal [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|advent stage]], so this option is not very accessible.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]/[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]: Very potent shield piercers that can help reduce Malevolent Jamiera's effective HP from 4 million down to 2.5 million.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman]]: His LD and massive damage vs traitless enemies means that he is an effective answer to the Dolphinas in the stage.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]: Strong against and able to slow Malevolent Jamiera as long as his shield is down. However, if you use him, make sure to build your lineup around surge immune units as he tends to trigger a lot of retaliatory surges.
*[[Pied Piper Cat (Rare Cat)|Brass Cat]]: A bizarre option that can support your anti-aku meatshields (like Cone Cat and Cactus Cat), their weaken can allow your tanky meatshields to survive way more hits from Malevolent Jamiera, coupled with their range (which is enough for them to safely hit a slowed down Malevolent Jamiera), they are guaranteed to make atleast some sort of impact, however, their mini-wave, while helpful, should be seen as a bonus in the event that a Li'l Doge runs up to them and makes Brass Cat hit him instead.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]]: Thanks to his relativly Low cost and fast recharge, he is very useful here.

